        "review": {
          "evidence": {
            "engineering-quality": {
              "availability": "available",
              "findings": [
                {
                  "evidence": "template/scripts/platform_divergence.py FrictionLog._load reports 'friction log ... does not exist' as an error, and every entry then gets a missing-friction-event problem. change-classes.md says to run the check 'where the event was recorded' but also suggests adding it to `full_commands`. The design.md decision 5 accepts this, but it makes the CI/full-validation placement contradictory for any project that has a hotfix.",
                  "id": "friction-log-machine-local-breaks-ci",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "The hotfix check requires the friction event id to exist in a machine-local log. A project with a valid hotfix would fail `platform_doctor.py` or the divergence check on CI or on any other machine than the one that recorded the event."
                },
                {
                  "evidence": "platform_divergence.py sha256_of uses path.read_bytes(); the manifest digests come from the LF template bytes, and the design assumes plain files are byte-identical downstream. There is no normalization and no diagnostic hint for this case.",
                  "id": "byte-digest-line-ending-sensitivity",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "Divergence detection compares raw-byte sha256 with the manifest. Checkout-time newline conversion (for example autocrlf or .gitattributes eol) would make every plain file look like an undeclared divergence or protected-touch."
                }
              ],
              "perspective": "engineering-quality",
              "report_sha256": "e1ded9de3be27b702141e90bac9fb9f7e965952fbb6b913d52fb2e466e90b719"
            },
            "spec-fidelity": {
              "availability": "available",
              "findings": [
                {
                  "evidence": "tasks.md 2.2 is marked [x] and requires wiring into 'the full-validation triggers in dev-platform/checks.toml'. design.md decision 6 says the project's `full_commands` trigger set includes the check. The diff changes only the source repo's dev-platform/checks.toml, and only to add test targets and the manifest --check. It adds no template checks entry that runs platform_divergence.py. change-classes.md says only that 'a project may also add it to the full_commands of its own project-owned checks",
                  "id": "full-validation-trigger-not-wired",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "The divergence check is not wired into the project's full-validation triggers. Task 2.2 and design decision 6 say it should be."
                },
                {
                  "evidence": "design.md decision 7 says `release_intent.py`/the release step regenerates the manifest. Task 1.1 says to generate it 'in the release preparation step'. The diff adds scripts/generate_platform_manifest.py, which must be run by hand with --write. It touches no release script. The only enforcement added is the platform test and `--check` in the docs checks.",
                  "id": "manifest-not-in-release-step",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "Manifest generation is not hooked into release preparation. A stale manifest is caught by a test and a docs check, not by the release step."
                },
                {
                  "evidence": "design.md decision 1: 'writes platform-manifest.json (path -> sha256, plus the release version)'. The spec says each platform release carries a manifest. The generated manifest has only `version` (the schema version 1), `files` and `project_harness_owned`, and generate_platform_manifest.py says 'The installed platform version is not stored here'. The stale check compares the entry's platform_version only with .dev-platform.toml platform_version. It cannot tell whether the manifest itself belongs",
                  "id": "manifest-lacks-release-version",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "The manifest does not carry the release version, though design decision 1 says it does. Stale detection instead trusts the local .dev-platform.toml."
                },
                {
                  "evidence": "template/dev-platform/protected-surface.toml removes scripts/agent_friction.py, execute_managed_task.py, orchestrate_pre_authoring.py, requirement_intake.py and requirement_retrospective.py, plus docs/README.md, from `hotfixable`. It adds the first five as new [[protected]] entries. It also protects platform_divergence.py and platform-manifest.json. proposal.md and the delta spec describe no change to the accepted protected-surface contract. The docs/README.md removal has no stated rationale. Th",
                  "id": "unproposed-protected-surface-reclassification",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "The change moves several files from hotfixable to protected and drops docs/README.md from hotfixable. The proposal, spec and tasks do not mention this."
                }
              ],
              "perspective": "spec-fidelity",
              "report_sha256": "636ec97c712c6441d978983a3f67756dbd696f3626c532e6812b2d5a2413c98c"
            }
          },
